WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.087
This is an important checkpoint.

00:00:02.087 --> 00:00:11.137
If you understand everything up to this point, you already understand the core architecture of RAG.

00:00:11.137 --> 00:00:16.137
On the indexing side, we clean documents, create chunks, and generate embeddings.

00:00:16.137 --> 00:00:25.987
On the question side, we embed the query, retrieve relevant chunks, build a prompt, and generate an answer with sources.

00:00:25.987 --> 00:00:30.087
Everything that follows is an improvement around this architecture.

00:00:30.799 --> 00:00:35.491
A vector database changes how vectors and metadata are stored and searched.

00:00:35.491 --> 00:00:39.091
Hybrid retrieval changes how candidates are ranked.

00:00:39.091 --> 00:00:42.651
Reranking improves the order of those candidates.

00:00:42.651 --> 00:00:46.296
Evaluation tells us whether changes actually help.

00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:49.811
But the core information flow remains the same.

00:00:49.811 --> 00:00:55.571
Before continuing, make sure you could explain this pipeline without looking at the code.

00:00:55.571 --> 00:01:02.041
If you can describe each stage and why it exists, you are ready for the more practical production-oriented parts of the

00:01:02.041 --> 00:01:03.198
module.
